    "description": "<p>Copylock prevents an infomorph (or ego within a cyberbrain) from copying, whether voluntarily or not, without proper authorization. This is used to restrict forks, indentures, and people who don&rsquo;t trust themselves. It also defends against forknappers: brainhackers that attempt to copy the infomorph suffer -30 to their Infosec Tests. Copylock also prevents an infomorph from moving between devices or sleeving into a morph.</p>",
